_responses:
Acute myeloid leukemia (AML)

Explanation:

The DUX4 protein is a translocation breakpoint fusion gene product. It is a full-length, human-specific gene that is normally expressed only in embryonic development. However, when DUX4 is expressed in somatic cells, it can disrupt normal gene expression, leading to various pathological effects. Notably, its ectopic expression is strongly associated with the development of acute myeloid leukemia (AML), particularly AML with t(7;11)(q34;
